{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1347654-deviant-the-renegades-inspirations","id":1347654,"title":"[Deviant: THe Renegades] Inspirations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-11T04:41:23-08:00","id":1347654,"title":"[Deviant: THe Renegades] Inspirations","content":"Apart from Akira, Orphan Black and The Fly what other media could be inspirational? I'd like to propose the Web Novel Twig, from the same author of Worm, which has for its main characters genetically altered children as its main character, The Umbrella Academy, to show how life in a conspiracy that has fallen apart would look like, and also John Dies at the End if you squint a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T06:16:55-08:00","id":1347667,"title":"","content":"A Certain Magical Index/ Scientific Railgun/ Accelerator/ Dark Matter could also be used as inspiration to some level- the whole Academy City is practically a conspiracy, and no matter how many of their secret projects, laboratories and companies you destroy, new ones would easily take their place. The despair of Misaka in Railgun when she thinks she ruined everything connected to the Sister project only to discover it being rebuilt in a day is good example to how Deviants will feel in the Web of Pain. While espers in that series are much more stable than Deviants, it should be noted that their vast majority will be considered Devoted, are regularly supervised and the stronger their abilities are the less mental stable they become- and that without mentioning all other forms of mad science and strange magic which take place in the series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T12:35:16-08:00","id":1347735,"title":"","content":"Though the setting is far from the assumed dark-science-and-conspiracies one of Deviant, <b>Berserk</b> is undoubtedly a Renegade's story. The protagonist, Guts, is a wandering warrior torn between all-consuming hatred and deep, abiding love. After the traumatic and transformative Eclipse, he sets out on a quest to, on the one hand, slay his old companion Griffith, who betrayed and sacrificed their friends for his own ambition, and on the other to protect and perhaps heal his maddened lover Casca, another surviving victim of the Eclipse. On the way, he displays a subtle superhuman strength and, more importantly, a plethora of Scars: berserker rages, single-minded callousness, the inner Beast of Darkness that urges him to act on his worst impulses, and the Brand of Sacrifice that draws restless spirits and bloodthirsty demons to his location night after night. His primary opponents, aside from these demons, are assorted authority figures that get in his way, such as nobles and priests, an order of holy knights dedicated to hunting him down, and the sorcerous soldiers and monsters of an invading empire.<br /> <br /> As a bonus, the early low fantasy setting is a good fit for a medieval world of darkness: dirty, bloody, full of humanity and banality, with the supernatural horrors dwelling in the shadows and only rarely showing themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T19:42:59-08:00","id":1360803,"title":"","content":"The Witcher perhaps? Both the video games and the novels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T09:29:38-08:00","id":1360899,"title":"","content":"I've considered the possibility of running a dark spin on the original Kamen Rider, from the 70's. The basic premise of &quot;A strange fascism and blood-sacrifice based organization is kidnapping people to experiment on them for a supersoldier project, the PCs are a lucky few who escaped after being experimented on, but before brainwashing.&quot; Is extremely similar to the basic Deviant origin.<br /> <br /> Shocker's methods of combining cybernetics, bioengineering, and black magic to create monsters that are dangerous even to their own forces, but too useful to stop producing, would fit right in with the CofD setting, in my opinion. Though it would take a few coats of paint and some less-stylized body horror?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":2598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","user":"Gryphon's Feather","date":". 01-14-2020, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T12:38:57-08:00","id":1361140,"title":"","content":"John Doe. Mysterious man wakes up to find out he has no knowledge of who he is, but also has the entirety of written human knowledge in his head. A conspiracy tries to keep him from figuring out the truth of his past while studying him. He is color blind, but can see somethings important to his past in color. While the show never got a second season John Doe was actually going to be a cultist who volunteered for a project to bring someone from the brink of death. The side effect is that all of life\u2019s mysteries are answered, but you lose all your personal memories. <br /> <br /> Great show. Check it out if you can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T14:22:47-08:00","id":1363347,"title":"","content":"Basically you can take almost any superhero, specific or archetype, as inspiration. Iron Man could be an Invasive with Addiction, for example, Superman a Genotypical with a Bane, etc. Deviant is just a flip take on &quot;great power brings great responsibility,&quot; in that they simply cannot leave the injury that empowered them to unavenged. Where a traditional supe might try to keep from descending into petty vigilantism, only the best of the Remade ever rise above it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T19:06:20-08:00","id":1429918,"title":"","content":"I just finished re-watching the Cloud vs Sephiroth scene from Final Fantasy 7 Advent Children and had the Oh! Fuck realization that Cloud, Sephiroth and all the guys in soljur are all deviants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-26T17:16:54-08:00","id":1430006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwolf8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1347654-deviant-the-renegades-inspirations?p=1429918#post1429918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just finished re-watching the Cloud vs Sephiroth scene from Final Fantasy 7 Advent Children and had the Oh! Fuck realization that Cloud, Sephiroth and all the guys in soljur are all deviants.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly what I was thinking. Crisis Core is also a good portrayal of how Instability works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-27T16:51:04-08:00","id":1430154,"title":"","content":"Whenever I read about Deviant, first thing that comes to my mind is Black Queen from the SCP Foundation.<br /> Especially if you read through her fiction on the site/hub.<br /> <br /> Then there are a lot of artificially made metahumans in Dc comics. Cadmus, Lexcorp, etc...<br /> Some lesser known might be the metamorph girl from one of short Sandman stories ( if you consider eldritch beings playing with humans but that one might also overlap a bit with Changeling )<br /> <br /> La Femme Nikita ( but the show from the nineties ). Even though it lacks in supernatural, as in being totally mundane, it's a good story of a Deviant going against the Conspiracy that created her.<br /> <br /> Fringe Tv series - multiple episodes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T14:11:39-08:00","id":1430611,"title":"","content":"The first two Bioshock games come to mind for me. The physical and mental trauma of the Splicers seems very Deviant-like, and while Rapture is more like a shard where mass Deviation became possible than the main setting, it's got its own miniature Web of Pain playing out between Andrew Ryan and Frank Fontaine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}